  "location": "East and Southeast Asia and the Pacific: China, Burma, Malaya, the Dutch East Indies, the Philippines, New Guinea, the Solomons, the Central Pacific, Japan and Manchuria",
  "wiki": "wiki/battles/pacific-war.md",
  "summary": "The war in Asia and the Pacific on one map, from Japan's invasion of China in 1937 to its surrender in 1945. After Pearl Harbor Japan overran Southeast Asia in five months, but Midway, Guadalcanal and the Kokoda Track stopped it. The Allies then advanced across the Central and South West Pacific and through Burma, destroyed the Japanese navy at the Philippine Sea and Leyte Gulf, took Iwo Jima and Okinawa, and burned Japan's cities from the air; the atomic bombs and the Soviet invasion of Manchuria brought surrender in August 1945.",
