      "time": "7–10 December 1941",
      "durationSec": 11,
      "narration": "On 7 December Nagumo's six carriers strike the US Pacific Fleet at Pearl Harbor: four battleships are sunk, 188 aircraft destroyed and 2,403 Americans killed, for 29 Japanese aircraft. Within hours Japan lands in Malaya and Thailand and bombs the Philippines; on 10 December land-based naval bombers sink the British battleship Prince of Wales and battlecruiser Repulse. Hong Kong falls on 25 December.",
